<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Felix Manz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1498–<a href="/years/1527">1527</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Felix Manz was a Swiss Anabaptist leader from Zürich and a former follower of Zwingli. With Conrad Grebel and George Blaurock he took part in the first adult baptisms in January 1525. Repeatedly imprisoned for preaching, he was drowned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limmat">Limmat</a> on 5 January 1527, the first Anabaptist executed by a Protestant authority.</p></div>
